    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>This is a guess based on past experience helping folks with h2o, you should check your application&#39;s logs to verify.</div><div><br></div>I believe that h2o will attempt to use memory based on what the host says it has, rather than how much the container the application is running in actually has available to it.<div>If you are running your application with the default &quot;large&quot; instance type, you have 1 GB of RAM available and you will need to initialize h2o with a lower maximum memory, otherwise h2o will exceed the memory limit and you should then see an &quot;out of memory&quot; error in the application&#39;s logs.</div></div>"
    ],
